## Overview

Customers is your address book for the people and businesses you sell to. Keep
one record for each customer so you can see who they are, how they like to pay
and what you have agreed with them, then pick them from the list whenever you
take an order.

## Tasks

### Add a new customer

1. Choose **New Customer** above the list.
2. Set **{field:customerType}** and **{field:status}** so you can tell new,
   regular and inactive customers apart.
3. Fill in the **{field:defaultShippingAddress}** and
   **{field:defaultBillingAddress}** so you do not have to type them again on
   every order.
4. Add **{field:paymentTerms}**, for example "Net 30", if you give this
   customer time to pay.
5. Save. The customer now shows up when you take a sales order.

### Keep track of what a customer can owe

1. Open the customer from the list and choose Edit.
2. Set **{field:creditLimit}** to the most you are comfortable letting them owe
   you at one time.
3. If you do not charge them sales tax, turn on **{field:taxExempt}** and enter
   their **{field:taxId}** so the number is on file.
4. Use **{field:notes}** for anything the next person who deals with this
   customer should know.

### Find a customer

Scan the list for the customer you want, or open a record to see everything you
have on file. To stop dealing with someone without losing their history, change
their **{field:status}** instead of deleting them.
